#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092036 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/id #uuid "0d1dcc59-e7af-5a86-87ba-aa7ee1b23767" :question/math-academy-id "e-632" :question/problem "Find the area bounded by the polar curve $r = \\cos(3\\theta)$ and the lines $\\theta = -\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ and $\\theta = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/350a721c254dab3a8acb2ae54ca5be0bcde6ab036e6936939194c57ae55fe4ff.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} r^2(\\theta) \\, \\textrm{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta) = \\cos(3\\theta),$ $\\theta_1=-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6},$ and $\\theta_2=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6},$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}{cos}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\theta {|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\theta ){|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}((\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}))+\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092037 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/id #uuid "6040d180-ed1d-52b8-809c-b5820352d3d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-633" :question/problem "Find the area bounded by the polar curve $r = 1+2\\cos\\theta$ for $\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3} \\leq \\theta \\leq \\dfrac{4\\pi}{3},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/6bfa0990b560bcb09f2a9eb0b9542296f2a8f1c196b6740702e81c59941d66c5.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} r^2(\\theta) \\, \\textrm{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta) = 1+2\\cos(\\theta),$ $\\theta_1=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3},$ and $\\theta_2=\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3},$ this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}(1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}(1+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+2\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{2\\pi /3}^{4\\pi /3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -4\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -3\\sqrt{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092052 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/id #uuid "a2d8dca5-a0f3-5b6f-81f5-4eea46ee70d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-6822" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/d7b39805131dc562e233d49a84f69d30e80ca29cb9443012032d18fdb4512054.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r = 2\\sin\\theta + 2\\cos\\theta$ for $\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\leq \\theta \\leq \\dfrac{3\\pi}{4},$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int_{\\theta_1}^{\\theta_2} r^2(\\theta) \\, \\textrm{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta) = 2\\sin\\theta + 2\\cos\\theta,$ $\\theta_1=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},$ and $\\theta_2=\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4},$ this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(4+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}) \\\\  & =2\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi -2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339895 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6eaa1bce-ed4a-5059-80f5-9db3c266a076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2+\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339897} {:answer/id #uuid "7604cab8-7de1-5507-acde-4a610e3f2045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339898} {:answer/id #uuid "e4455fd3-b174-5cc7-8e84-d28cd5cfaa21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339899} {:answer/id #uuid "e9d3a11b-9d7d-5e3b-8b07-4f8da55a9665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡(4\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339900} {:answer/id #uuid "1b641633-da1e-5cf0-97ed-1fe5a2629c95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b641633-da1e-5cf0-97ed-1fe5a2629c95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339901} :answer-field/id #uuid "52abf03f-5f90-5c5b-bc10-e06429cac772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bda350c7-482c-5619-afeb-e65f12cc1277" :question/math-academy-id "q-123889" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the area bounded by the graph of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b88d8d3-eeb7-580e-a603-9e69573a1364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(\\theta +3)\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339904} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa68d79-3958-584f-a639-a00ef154466c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339905} {:answer/id #uuid "214cac02-b79c-52c7-85d0-b81b5dee4f4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(9\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339906} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c144c8-257c-5063-85ad-60bdef23ee00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339907} {:answer/id #uuid "97cb1893-7c41-55dc-a1d9-03ad7f6be1c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0c144c8-257c-5063-85ad-60bdef23ee00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339907} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc386da6-5dbb-5713-8184-3cb035187ec3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "297129bb-a339-52f1-bb28-be479ab08064" :question/math-academy-id "q-123892" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the area bounded by graph of the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )$ for $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "288889f1-b41b-5ed9-bb95-86ad6c731b71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339911} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8d815a-1db8-5984-8c56-a36de66791a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339912} {:answer/id #uuid "9f142702-5dff-5216-be6b-82ca122b2853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339913} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb7a604-0b9c-512a-b7a5-9a0e1e1d1aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25\\pi }{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339914} {:answer/id #uuid "ea7bf6b3-959f-55c5-8aca-44a219064e25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb7a604-0b9c-512a-b7a5-9a0e1e1d1aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25\\pi }{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339914} :answer-field/id #uuid "17946a64-87f8-5534-a0c6-3bb8e37bbb44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3c44d6f-636b-5b6d-91fb-4a2eb41efe61" :question/math-academy-id "q-123894" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/7a48288304608aa9d2b68a34794183cf58308ce16487c1675318180936868674.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$ for $\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{5\\pi }{4},$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\pi $ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}(\\theta {|}_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta ){|}_{\\pi }^{5\\pi /4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}((\\frac{5\\pi }{4}-(\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{25\\pi }{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92cdebf8-0836-5c7e-9da6-15c1f702e823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4})}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339917} {:answer/id #uuid "64d2b62b-6b73-53f0-8bca-953eef617799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4})}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339918} {:answer/id #uuid "c35d0eee-87d2-5b30-8a52-13c4d3242674" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4})}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339919} {:answer/id #uuid "9737a530-030d-59b6-bdd5-f8e401009f93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4})\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339920} {:answer/id #uuid "02a58311-7a4b-5e80-b15c-9266de79ff69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4})\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92cdebf8-0836-5c7e-9da6-15c1f702e823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4})}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339917} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f80a905-e40c-5fbf-8a55-e9f7f1978494" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aeb48f66-6646-5fa1-b59e-10910893bf80" :question/math-academy-id "q-14866" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the total area enclosed by the graph of the polar curve $r=1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4}$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ?$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4}$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=2\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )}{4})}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc9dc3b-e2d2-5b3a-9013-393bc9646d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339924} {:answer/id #uuid "718da9d6-2b7d-5651-9adb-e243e800e73b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339925} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd30146-a432-589f-a44b-73ed14899f70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/val