knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c16d0e2-f600-56a4-a844-e0c981a38158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339931} {:answer/id #uuid "09aea622-558d-5eb6-aa78-4852385868b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c16d0e2-f600-56a4-a844-e0c981a38158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339931} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4bddb98-6829-5cd2-945b-a0864a4a8925" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f45c70c3-95c4-5d62-96ce-c5622e2bdba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-352284" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}-\\frac{9}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{9}{8}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "974a88f6-ff6a-5183-aeaf-6019e09061ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by a Petal of a Polar Rose"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b412b100-137b-5261-92af-08adb0e78ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{8}+\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b412b100-137b-5261-92af-08adb0e78ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi}{8}+\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339935} :answer-field/id #uuid "f28c30ed-7af0-5f7c-8b7e-585d920484af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1978d58f-4d27-5cb2-a88a-4942c49c5a7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-352303" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}+\\frac{9}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))+\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{9}{8}(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{8}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi +18}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c01212c-46cb-5c89-a799-d31c025f2517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi}{2}-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339938} {:answer/id #uuid "94cd5c5f-7d96-50cb-ac99-e3cebbfafd5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c01212c-46cb-5c89-a799-d31c025f2517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27\\pi}{2}-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339938} :answer-field/id #uuid "5eed3487-2daa-5674-866a-14261a8a8299" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c39bcd1-887c-5842-addf-0cba732da132" :question/math-academy-id "q-352319" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/4f3086c30f3c442e19e0844311b9ee57a75a517496861380a8bf3836c5adb539.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=5+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\pi \\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=5+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\pi $ and ${\\theta }_{2}=2\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(5+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(25+20\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(25+20\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(27\\theta -20\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(27\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }-20\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }-10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}(2\\pi -\\pi )-10(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi }{2}-10(1-(-1))-\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\pi }{2}-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d13fdb-ad7a-5612-bc7d-5f5540ec3dcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7d13fdb-ad7a-5612-bc7d-5f5540ec3dcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339942} :answer-field/id #uuid "45515d57-411e-5249-b51c-2935ed03ce75" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47c4e623-f4aa-593d-8c75-d6588f55fae9" :question/math-academy-id "q-352323" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=4+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=4+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(4+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(16+16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}(16+16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(18\\theta -16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )){|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(18\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}\\,) \\\\  & =9\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =9(\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6})-8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =3\\pi -8(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03344200-7948-5019-9dfd-49d98748cd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339945} {:answer/id #uuid "89d40137-edc5-5668-a944-6e0d03ddfc7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03344200-7948-5019-9dfd-49d98748cd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339945} :answer-field/id #uuid "acf766d9-60e8-506e-b773-5ec36fa788a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0aa3c96c-3a12-54be-a246-58cadfe8bbe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-352330" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/327f1f7a395616de463c054ec904812dcd422776522a262f956530d3aa9278eb.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }4{\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\theta }^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{\\theta }^{3}}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3})-2(\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e2f1d39-0c8b-55df-8de9-b97ef0fe5da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3e^2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e2f1d39-0c8b-55df-8de9-b97ef0fe5da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3e^2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339949} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9674210-a3aa-534e-a1af-a681c694254a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8950de2c-8595-511b-8c63-6801ecf35ee7" :question/math-academy-id "q-352337" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r={e}^{\\theta +1}$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )={e}^{\\theta +1}$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{({e}^{\\theta +1})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{e}^{2\\theta +2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{e}^{2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{2\\theta }}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}({e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}(4-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcfd0e40-b327-505a-a3bf-67837f9b1f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8e^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339952} {:answer/id #uuid "bf4e0c89-ed9b-5492-b94e-37cca1f24084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4e^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcfd0e40-b327-505a-a3bf-67837f9b1f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8e^2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339952} :answer-field/id #uuid "78cffae8-2374-54b1-9142-284c31b23b6f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9bc37aca-125c-56a1-af2c-6a1af9e536d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-352338" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2{e}^{1-\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2{e}^{1-\\theta }$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}(2{e}^{1-\\theta })^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}4{e}^{2-2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{e}^{-2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}(-\\frac{{e}^{-2\\theta }}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2}({e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-{e}^{2}(\\frac{1}{9}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bab9a6ea-ef29-5c02-935a-cfa5077c9311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339956} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9816ab-9ea9-50b3-9c69-124623aa4db4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a9816ab-9ea9-50b3-9c69-124623aa4db4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339957} :answer-field/id #uuid "fde7407a-6958-59d3-8aa6-2f5aee46a927" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1aca8a53-e45a-51aa-87f5-6f1b927c4b18" :question/math-academy-id "q-352343" :question/problem "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ ${\\theta }_{1}=0,$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\frac{3}{2}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3}{2}\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{3}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }\\,) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{8}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(\\pi -0)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-0+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c9f0f1-be39-5893-b757-7a4750b07ab5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Bounded by the Loop of a Limaçon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acbf3d13-ad2d-554e-9617-2c42abfb3800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi +16}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339960} {:answer/id #uuid "d6671d9e-eca7-50b9-bb45-cc152dfb4842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339961} {:answer/id #uuid "dde14f6a-b929-5100-937b-da6cbcccf0e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi -6}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339962} {:answer/id #uuid "c4940a9a-825f-5245-855e-ceb1f3c3c211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi -8}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339963} {:answer/id #uuid "71c8bd58-fc14-5181-8274-fee54511e6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi -16}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71c8bd58-fc14-5181-8274-fee54511e6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi -16}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339964} :answer-field/id #uuid "16b084c8-a495-5d0e-8bfc-81ebd2fcecc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0b4c5d8-d21f-5ce8-b0e4-b418ee1b837a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79807" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060520/assets/f57ddfb02991296cbc0280272aa1a28e36cfed926dfedcd7b1955868cf83fff5.png)\n\nFind the area bounded by the polar curve $r=2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(4-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}(\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi })) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )}{8}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\pi -0)+2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}+2(-2)-\\frac{1}{8}(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi -16}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a62e8412-1733-577c-bd60-25395e6fa908" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Areas Bounded by Other Polar Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c238f3f-945f-5153-